this is conor mcgregor born into a  working-class family from the suburbs of  dublin at one point he was a plumber  living on social welfare in 2021 forbes  named him the highest paid athlete in  the world that year he had a net worth  of 180 million dollars conor mcgregor is  one of the most dominant fighters in ufc  history a two division champion in ufc  he was for a time considered the king of  combat sports living a lavish life and  earning a nine-figure payday with the  help of a dubious boxing match against  floyd money mayweather but while  mcgregor took naturally to the superstar  life it wasn't something he was born  into coming from a working-class family  from the suburbs of dublin he journeyed  his way through childhood gyms a stint  as a plumber's apprentice and eventual  worldwide fame as the most notorious  fighter on the planet and the biggest  name in the ufc this is the story of  mcgregor's rise to the top of the world  conor mcgregor was born on july 14 1988  he would spend his youth in kremlin a  suburb of dublin in dublin he would meet  his now longtime coach john cavanaugh  after going into one of kavanaugh's gyms  mcgregor beat up two of the best  fighters there in a sparring session  that he took a bit too seriously  kavanaugh responded by pinning him and  throwing heavy blows until conor  promised he was there for training and  not for a street brawl  uninterested in school he took to  plumbing as a trade and did what he  could to make a living for some time  there were times when he would work  12-hour days before heading to the gym  to train as a fighter it was around this  time that he started dating his longtime  girlfriend dee devlin  when he gave up plumbing to train  full-time his parents disapproved of the  decision so much so he and his father  came to blows he told his father that  he'll be a self-made millionaire by the  age of 25. mcgregor took part in his  first mma match in march 2008 for the  london-based promotion cage warriors  defeating gary morris by tko in the  second round  he would go four and two through his  first six fights before starting the  winning streak that would take him to  international fame during that run of  early fights mcgregor attended his first  ever ufc event and caught chuck  liddell's attention long enough to snag  a selfie it's the type of encounter  mcgregor would soon find himself on the  other side of often  after his 4-2 start conor would win his  next eight fights all within the first  two rounds and become a two-division  champion of cage warriors buzz continued  to grow and he was eventually booked for  his first fight with ufc  on april 6 2013 mcgregor made his ufc  debut against marcus brimage winning by  knockout in the first round just a week  before that fight he had picked up a  welfare check for 188 euros to help him  get by but mcgregor took home the prize  for knockout of the night and the 60 000  bonus that came with it later in life he  would name his boat the 188 in memory of  those checks  ufc president dana white was immediately  impressed with mcgregor he said he was  blown away by mcgregor's debut in  stockholm it was the beginning of a  profitable relationship from there  conor's run of dominance continued  he won five more fights four of which  didn't make it through two rounds he  beat chad mendez and claimed the interim  ufc featherweight championship this put  mcgregor in a position to face jose aldo  in a unification bout for the ufc  featherweight championship  in the lead-up to the fight mcgregor  said he was going to unify the belts  destroy the featherweight division and  take the lightweight division as well  on december 12 2015 mcgregor knocked out  jose aldo in just 13 seconds it was the  fastest finish ever for a ufc title  fight again it was his unstoppable left  that did the job  true to his word mcgregor set out to win  in the lightweight division and a fight  with rafael dos anos for the title was  set for ufc 196 in march but dos anjos  had to withdraw after breaking his foot  leading former lightweight contender  nate diaz to step up on short notice to  face mcgregor  diaz had been training as a welterweight  at 170 pounds and mcgregor decided he  would again gain the weight to meet him  there jumping two weight classes in just  two weeks  mcgregor was the heavy favorite going  into the fight but would get caught in  the second round and end up tapping out  after diaz locked in a rear naked choke  hold giving mcgregor the first loss of  his ufc career despite his shocking loss  to nate diaz in 2016 mcgregor became the  first mixed martial artist to appear on  forbes list of the hundred highest paid  athletes taking 22 million dollars on  the year between his fights with diaz  aldo and a variety of sponsorships after  a series of negotiations that included  mcgregor being dropped from the ufc 200  for refusing to go on a press tour  promoting the fight mcgregor ds2 was set  for ufc 202. the fight was a bloodbath  thrilling fans around the world it would  go down as one of mcgregor's most  memorable performances in the octagon in  the end both fighters would once again  receive fight of the night honours with  connor winning by majority decision  just three months later he would  challenge eddie alvarez for the ufc  lightweight championship the fight was  set for ufc 205  in the prelude to the fight mcgregor  showed his normal confidence telling his  opponent to show up so he could break  his face  conor would win by tko in the second  round and became the first ever fighter  to hold ufc titles in multiple divisions  after the win mcgregor said that he  would take time off from fighting to  wait for the birth of his child during  that time off mcgregor began pushing for  a boxing match against mayweather rumors  that negotiations were underway began  swirling a month later it was announced  that the fight was officially on  mayweather and mcgregor would meet in  the ring in las vegas for what would  surely be the biggest fight of the year  mcgregor made the announcement official  with a post on instagram trolling the  undefeated boxer the bill to the fight  on august 26 was fast and furious both  mayweather and mcgregor set out on a  four city tour to promote the fight  trading verbal jabs and obscenities  along the way  at the next confrontation in front of a  particularly frisky crowd in toronto  mcgregor called out mayweather's rumored  illiteracy much to the delight of those  who had gathered to watch the press  conference experts didn't give mcgregor  much of a chance to beat mayweather with  former champion mike tyson saying  mcgregor going gonna get killed  additionally some mocked mcgregor for  training sessions he made public  especially his bag work and his warm-up  routine  mcgregor never really stood a chance  against mayweather and was eventually  dispatched by tko in the 10th round but  despite the loss mcgregor was still  surely pleased with the result earning a  rumored 100 million dollars for his role  in the circus of a fight  after the mayweather fight mcgregor took  a bit more time off to enjoy his riches  he went to the 2018 world cup final and  did so as a personal guest of russian  president vladimir putin conor mcgregor  announced the launch of his whiskey  brand in 2017. a year later the irishman  launched the brand with the name proper  12. proper 12 irish whiskey became conor  mcgregor's first business venture  outside combat sports riding on the  sportsman's showmanship the brand  generated around 1 billion dollars in  revenue just in the first year of its  sales  but soon enough there was reason to  tease his return to the ufc his natural  opponent was khabib the undefeated  russian fighter who had taken over as  champion of the lightweight division in  mcgregor's absence things came to a head  when mcgregor bizarrely attacked a bus  khabib was on ahead of ufc 223 leading  to several injuries to other fighters  mcgregor would later explain that he was  acting to protect his teammate artem  loboff who was confronted by khabib at a  hotel mcgregor would be taken into  custody and charged with an assault for  his attack but ultimately got off  relatively unscathed and thus the stage  was set for a fight between mcgregor and  khabib for the ufc lightweight title  ufc even used footage of mcgregor's  attack on the bus to promote the  upcoming fight  at the fight khabib dominated mcgregor  eventually forcing him to tap out in the  fourth round  when the final bell rang khabib would  leap out of the octagon and start a  brawl with some of mcgregor's teammates  resulting in suspensions for both  fighters  despite the loss mcgregor was expected  to return to the octagon in 2019 having  signed a six-fight deal with the ufc  ahead of the khabib fight instead  mcgregor shockingly announced his  retirement from fighting in march 2019  but as is often the case mcgregor's  retirement didn't stick and he began  needling for a rematch with khabib but  there were other fighters in line for a  title shot though meaning mcgregor would  have to wait his turn  in the meantime mcgregor had more  trouble with the law in march of 2019  mcgregor was arrested after an encounter  with a fan in miami slapping a phone out  of his hand and stomping on it then in  april mcgregor reportedly punched an  older man in a dublin pub after he  refused a shot of the irish fighter's  whiskey eventually mcgregor started  focusing on his return to ufc long-time  ufc contender donald cowboy cerrone  emerged as a potential opponent mcgregor  made quick work of cerrone knocking the  cowboy out in just 40 seconds after  opening the fight with a devastating  shoulder charge and ending it with a  brutal series of punches  after the fight mcgregor paid respect to  his opponent and even embraced cowboy's  grandmother in the octagon a few months  after the fight mcgregor announced his  retirement once again but it wouldn't  last long  by august he was teasing another  potential superstar boxing bout this  time against manny pacquiao but by  october his next ufc bout was in the  works setting up a rematch against  dustin poirier on fight island mcgregor  previously beat poirier in 2014 winning  via first round knockout the two faced  off again at ufc 257  with poirier winning by tko in round two  the internet had a field day with  mcgregor's loss as he became a meme  dubbed sleepy mcgregor  the two then faced off again for the  much-anticipated trilogy fight at ufc  264. poirier again won by tko with  mcgregor breaking his leg at the end of  round one the post-fight interview  became one of mcgregor's most legendary  moments in ufc history  outside of fighting his whiskey business  became a success proper 12 was the  sponsor of the deontay wilder vs tyson  fury 2 fight in 2018 mcgregor and the  ufc signed a six-fight contract that  also included a proper 12 presence as a  sponsor for every card the irishman  fights on in 2020 proper 12 became the  fourth most popular irish whiskey brand  globally in terms of sales proximo  spirits acquired the majority stake of  proper 12 in a 600 million deal it is  unclear how much conor mcgregor made  directly through the deal but it's going  to be quite substantial he still hasn't  retired from fighting yet after poirier  there's plenty of other opponents  mcgregor might take on  he's repeatedly expressed a desire for  another shot at now retired champion  khabib  mcgregor has also been tied to a  potential return to boxing where a fight  against manny pacquiao could potentially  net 250 million dollars there's no  telling what the future holds for  mcgregor  in every journey to success there's a  lesson to be learned so what can we  learn from mcgregor's rise to the top  his genius lies in his ability to  leverage media attention there's no  doubt he's an incredible fighter and has  helped the ufc become much more  mainstream critics will often point out  that he's too controversial overdramatic  and trash talks too much  however that's the exact reason why he's  become so successful  we live in an attention economy he is a  master at getting attention and  generating media hype in the fight game  people don't want to see two fighters  get on stage shaking hands they want the  drama the hype and the trash talking  it's the buzz around the fight that  makes it exciting and if that hype  brings in viewers and media attention no  matter if mcgregor wins or loses he  still gets a massive payday with all  that attention he's become his own brand  ultimately making him incredibly rich  and successful  thanks for staying till the end of this  video if you enjoyed this video then be  sure to hit the like button drop a  comment subscribe and hit the  notification bell for more content like  this  also be sure to check out our other  videos on this channel links are in the  description and we'll see you in the  next one
 

